So it is more or less a question of how you value different aspects of 
the game experience.  You seem to look at early characters as expendable 
and this is a valid point of view.  I consider each single character as 
a challenge to be met and try to have him survive.  (One reason I play 
conducts very rarely.)

Now when you say that you think you have a 4 to 1 ratio of death to 
survival that means that your ascension rate will be below 20% with this 
strategy (because some of the characters that do survive the racket may 
still not ascend).  My ascension rate averaged over all classes is 
somewhere between 25% and 30%, so the racket is not a viable alternative 
to me.

